    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Echinoderms display a unique symmetry shift: larvae are bilaterally symmetrical, whereas adults exhibit radial symmetry.",
        "Nematodes (Aschelminthes) are the only pseudocoelomates; Platyhelminthes are acoelomate, and Annelids onwards are true coelomates.",
        "Aves possess pneumatic (air-filled) long bones for flight adaptation, while mammals are uniquely characterized by mammary glands."
      ],
      "id": "2f82w8k"
    },
